│   15     """Serialize `record` to a canonical, deterministic one-line JSON string.                                                                          │
│   16                                                                                                                                                        │
│   17     stdlib `json.dumps(record, sort_keys=True, separators=_SEPARATORS)` returns a                                                                      │
│   18     compact string with keys sorted and no extra whitespace, using the exact                                                                           │
│   19     separators given (",", ":").                                                                                                                       │
│   20                                                                                                                                                        │
│   21     `ujson.dumps` does not accept a `separators` kwarg at all (passing it raises                                                                       │
│   22     a TypeError), and it already emits compact output (no spaces after "," or                                                                          │
│   23     ":") by default, so the compact-separator behavior is preserved without                                                                            │
│   24     needing to specify it. It does, however, accept `sort_keys`, which is                                                                              │
│   25     required here for deterministic, byte-reproducible audit logs -- but older                                                                         │
│   26     ujson releases have had inconsistent support for that flag, so we defend                                                                           │
