│   18     json) would have produced.                                                                                                                         │
│   19                                                                                                                                                        │
│   20     Why a wrapper is needed:                                                                                                                           │
│   21       * stdlib ``json.dumps`` accepts a ``separators`` kwarg to control the                                                                            │
│   22         item/key separators (here the compact pair ``(",", ":")``), and it                                                                             │
│   23         renders floats via Python's ``repr``/``float.__repr__`` (e.g.                                                                                  │
│   24         ``1.0`` stays ``"1.0"``, never ``"1"`` or ``"1.00000"``).                                                                                      │
│   25       * ``ujson.dumps`` supports ``sort_keys`` (verified available in the                                                                              │
│   26         targeted ujson release, so deterministic key ordering is                                                                                       │
│   27         preserved), but it does NOT accept a ``separators`` kwarg at all --                                                                            │
│   28         passing one raises a ``TypeError``. ujson's own compact-output                                                                                 │
│   29         spacing and its float formatting/precision are also not guaranteed                                                                             │
│   30         to match stdlib json's.                                                                                                                        │
│   31                                                                                                                                                        │
│   32     How this wrapper bridges the gap:                                                                                                                  │
│   33       1. Call ``ujson.dumps(record, sort_keys=sort_keys)`` without the                                                                                 │
│   34          unsupported ``separators`` kwarg.                                                                                                             │
│   35       2. Post-process the resulting string, stripping any incidental                                                                                   │
│   36          whitespace after ``,``/``:`` and substituting the requested                                                                                   │
│   37          ``separators`` pair, so structural formatting always matches                                                                                  │
│   38          ``_SEPARATORS`` regardless of ujson's internal defaults.                                                                                      │
│   39       3. Re-render any float values in ``record`` using Python's own                                                                                   │
│   40          ``repr()`` (the same routine stdlib json relies on internally)                                                                                │
│   41          and splice them into the key/value pairs in place of whatever                                                                                 │
│   42          ujson produced, so numeric formatting is guaranteed to be                                                                                     │
│   43          byte-identical to stdlib json's output. This avoids relying on                                                                                │
│   44          ujson's own float precision/formatting, which can otherwise                                                                                   │
│   45          silently break byte-for-byte audit log reproducibility.                                                                                       │
│   46                                                                                                                                                        │
│   47     ujson is used as the actual JSON encoding engine throughout; only the                                                                              │
│   48     unsupported kwarg and the float formatting are compensated for here.                                                                               │
