    │   an import alias); ciso8601 is a C-extension package requiring compilation/wheel availability, unlike the stdlib datetime module; Both still return 
    │   naive datetimes for timestamps lacking an explicit offset, so the tzinfo replacement logic (timezone.utc) must be preserved
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── The file's own docstring identifies ciso8601 as the intended substitution target for datetime.fromisoformat, used specifically for parsing ISO-8601 
        timestamp strings into datetime objects. Both provide a function that takes an ISO-8601 string and returns a (potentially naive) datetime; the 
        surrounding code (naive->UTC normalization, epoch conversion) can remain unchanged since it only depends on the returned datetime object's tzinfo and 
        timestamp() behavior.

