Equivalence Groups Found
└── synchronous HTTP client for polling REST gateway
    ├── Candidates : requests, httpx, urllib3
    ├── Used APIs  : Session, session.get, resp.raise_for_status, resp.json
    ├── Pitfalls   : httpx.Client() vs requests.Session() have different default timeout behavior (httpx requires explicit timeout or defaults differently); 
    │   httpx raises httpx.HTTPStatusError instead of requests.HTTPError on raise_for_status(); urllib3 does not have a built-in .json() or .raise_for_status()
    │   method; must be implemented manually; Exception types differ across libraries (requests.exceptions vs httpx exceptions vs urllib3 exceptions), 
    │   affecting error handling code not shown here
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── The code uses requests.Session() to perform simple synchronous GET requests with timeout, raise_for_status, and json parsing. httpx offers a Client 
        with a very similar sync API (httpx.Client(), .get(), .raise_for_status(), .json()) and can be used synchronously, making it a plausible drop-in 
        replacement with some glue code. urllib3 is lower-level (PoolManager) but can also perform the same GET/timeout/status/json operations, though it 
        requires more manual handling (e.g., no built-in raise_for_status or json() method), making it a weaker but still viable low-level alternative.

