Equivalence Groups Found
└── synchronous HTTP client for polling REST gateway
    ├── Candidates : requests, httpx
    ├── Used APIs  : Session, session.get, resp.raise_for_status, resp.json
    ├── Pitfalls   : httpx.Client() vs requests.Session() have different constructor defaults (e.g., timeout defaults, connection pooling config); Exception 
    │   types differ: requests raises requests.exceptions.HTTPError/ConnectionError, httpx raises httpx.HTTPStatusError/httpx.RequestError; timeout semantics 
    │   differ: requests timeout is per-request float or tuple, httpx timeout can be a Timeout object with granular read/write/connect settings; httpx defaults
    │   to raising on redirects differently and has stricter typing for URLs
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── requests.Session() is used to issue synchronous GET requests with a timeout, check status, and parse JSON. httpx provides a near drop-in sync Client 
        with equivalent methods (get, raise_for_status, json) and can be used in fully synchronous mode, making it a viable substitute for this specific usage 
        pattern.

