Equivalence Groups Found
└── synchronous HTTP client for polling REST endpoints
    ├── Candidates : requests, httpx
    ├── Used APIs  : Session, session.get, resp.raise_for_status, resp.json
    ├── Pitfalls   : httpx.Client() vs requests.Session() have different default timeout behavior (requests has no default timeout, httpx defaults to 5s); 
    │   Exception types differ: requests.exceptions.HTTPError vs httpx.HTTPStatusError, and connection errors have different class hierarchies; httpx.Client 
    │   requires explicit close() or context manager use for proper resource cleanup, differing from requests.Session lifecycle expectations; Session 
    │   construction signatures differ slightly (e.g., auth, adapters, mounting) if those features are later added
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── The file uses requests.Session() to perform synchronous GET requests against a SCADA gateway, check status codes, and parse JSON. httpx provides a 
        nearly identical sync API (httpx.Client(), .get(), .raise_for_status(), .json()) and can be used in fully synchronous mode, making it a legitimate 
        drop-in substitute for this use case. The docstring itself calls this out as the intended substitution target.

