synchronous public methods, and converting them to async would change TelemetryBridge's public API, which the migration explicitly must avoid.
    - amqtt's publish() coroutine does not return a paho-style MQTTMessageInfo object with an 'rc' attribute; the getattr(info, 'rc', 0) pattern has no direct 
analogue in amqtt's return values, so 'rc' semantics would have to be fabricated/faked rather than genuinely migrated.
    - connect() semantics differ structurally: paho's connect(host, port) is a synchronous blocking call with implicit reconnect/keepalive handling, while 
amqtt's connect() is an async coroutine typically expecting a broker URI and asyncio event-loop context, with different QoS negotiation and reconnection 
behavior — a wrapper can shim the call signature but cannot replicate the blocking guarantees the rest of the code (and its callers) depend on.
    - Running amqtt's async client synchronously via ad hoc event-loop driving (e.g., one loop.run_until_complete per call) is not a supported usage pattern of
the library and risks event-loop/transport lifecycle issues, meaning no wrapper can honestly claim full equivalence — this is a structural execution-model gap,
not a glue-code gap.

