    │   call, so the EmailNotifier class and its dependency-injected `smtp` object would need a compatibility shim/connector.; apprise does not expose a 
    │   per-call sender/recipient list the same way; recipients/sender must be encoded in the apprise URL or Apprise object configuration ahead of time.; 
    │   Testability pattern here (injecting a smtp object with .sendmail) does not map directly onto apprise's Apprise() instance/notify() flow.; apprise pulls
    │   in many optional service dependencies; smtplib is stdlib-only with zero extra dependencies.
    ├── Constraints: requires_connector
    └── The file's own docstring identifies apprise as the intended substitution target for smtplib-based email notification. Both can deliver an 
        alarm/notification message to recipients, but apprise abstracts over many notification services (email, Slack, etc.) via a unified `notify()` call 
        rather than smtplib's SMTP-protocol-specific `sendmail()`/`SMTP()` object model.

