    - apprise's mailto:// URL scheme typically expects credentials (user/pass) or at least a fully qualified relay target; host/port alone (as used by smtplib 
for anonymous/local relay) may not map cleanly onto every apprise mailto configuration and may require additional configuration input not present in the 
original code.
    - apprise pulls in numerous optional third-party service dependencies at install time versus smtplib's zero-dependency stdlib nature — an 
operational/packaging concern, not an API-compatibility blocker.
    - The dependency-injection testability pattern (injecting a fake `smtp` object with `.sendmail`) must be preserved manually by ensuring the wrapper/shim's 
public surface (`sendmail(sender, recipients, message)`) is stable and mockable in tests; this is achievable but requires discipline in the wrapper's design 
rather than being automatic.

